  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"0.5.1\"\n\npackage:\n  name: tera-cli\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/chevdor/tera-cli/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: ec5cffd2458a23f0bbd80f6394e8f42b07e9d3efd258816e726aa4909c7ccc0e\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  script:\n    env:\n      CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_LTO: fat\n      CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_STRIP: symbols\n    interpreter: nu\n    content:\n      - let prefix = $env.LIBRARY_PREFIX? | default $env.PREFIX\n      # build main app and generate license data\n      - cargo auditable install --path=. --root=($prefix) --no-track --locked --bins --features=full\n      - cargo-bundle-licenses --format=yaml --output=THIRDPARTY.yml\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('rust') }}\n    - cargo-auditable\n    - cargo-bundle-licenses\n    - nushell\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - tera --help\n      - tera --version\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - tera\n      strict: true\n\nabout:\n  summary: CLI for rendering Tera templates using JSON, YAML, TOML, and environment variables\n  description: |\n    tera-cli (providing the `tera` command) is a command-line utility built on\n    top of the Rust-based [Tera](https://keats.github.io/tera/) templating\n    engine inspired by Jinja2 and Django. It merges structured context data\n    (from JSON, YAML, or TOML files) and system environment variables into\n    template files to generate rendered outputs.\n  license: MIT\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - THIRDPARTY.yml\n  homepage: https://github.com/chevdor/tera-cli\n  repository: https://github.com/chevdor/tera-cli\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - salim-b\n",
